diff --git a/RUN_SCALEALIGN.md b/RUN_SCALEALIGN.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..616ff4a8364c71d2bdf7fd2644a4f27c0028c061
--- /dev/null
+++ b/RUN_SCALEALIGN.md
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+# ScaleAlign Experiment Runbook
+
+The project uses the CUDA 12.1 PyTorch environment already available at
+`../rf-detr/.venv-scalealign`. Run all commands from this directory.
+
+Every S/M/L run loads the same official COCO-trained DINO R50 five-scale
+checkpoint. The backbone is not randomly initialized and torchvision does not
+download a second ImageNet checkpoint during construction. Backbone, encoder,
+decoder, prediction heads, and ScaleAlign are all trainable. A physical batch
+of one with 16-step gradient accumulation reproduces DINO five-scale's official
+effective batch size of 16 on the single available GPU.
+
+## 1. Prepare data
+
+```bash
+../rf-detr/.venv-scalealign/bin/python -u tools/prepare_scalealign_data.py
+```
+
+This reuses the existing COCO 2017 directory, resumes missing archives, and
+creates COCO-format VOC and VisDrone annotations under `data/`.
+
+## 2. Verify the GPU
+
+```bash
+nvidia-smi -L
+../rf-detr/.venv-scalealign/bin/python -c \
+  "import torch; print(torch.__version__, torch.version.cuda, torch.cuda.is_available())"
+```
+
+Do not start the matrix unless `torch.cuda.is_available()` prints `True`.
+The implementation automatically uses a differentiable PyTorch CUDA fallback
+when the optional native deformable-attention extension is unavailable. This is
+functionally complete but slower than compiling the extension with CUDA 12.1.
+
+## 3. Run all nine experiments
+
+```bash
+MPLCONFIGDIR=/tmp/matplotlib-scalealign \
+../rf-detr/.venv-scalealign/bin/python -u tools/run_scalealign_matrix.py
+```
+
+Run one experiment by restricting both dimensions:
+
+```bash
+../rf-detr/.venv-scalealign/bin/python -u tools/run_scalealign_matrix.py \
+  --datasets coco --sizes s
+```
+
+The launcher skips a run with `checkpoint_best_regular.pth` and DINO resumes
+an interrupted run automatically from `checkpoint.pth`.
+
+## 4. Build the result table
+
+```bash
+../rf-detr/.venv-scalealign/bin/python tools/report_scalealign.py
+```
+
+Outputs are written to `reports/scalealign_results.{md,csv,json}`. Rows remain
+`pending` until evaluator metrics exist; the reporter never invents results.
